{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghW2cJvdvDpxnixPJEMx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 520 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 700 cm⁻¹**, from the two upper bands alone. The lowest band does not fit this model well (see the check below).\n\n**Assignment.** The ground state of tetrahedral d⁷ is ⁴A₂(F). The three bands are:\n- ν₁ = ⁴T₂(F) ← ⁴A₂, at 4 330 cm⁻¹\n- ν₂ = ⁴T₁(F) ← ⁴A₂, at 7 520 cm⁻¹\n- ν₃ = ⁴T₁(P) ← ⁴A₂, at 18 640 cm⁻¹\n\n**Model.** ⁴T₂ does not mix with any other state, so its energy is exactly 10Dq. The two ⁴T₁ states mix through the matrix [[6Dq, 6B], [6B, 15B]]. Energies are measured from the ⁴A₂ ground state, which lies at −12Dq. That gives the eigenvalues λ = ν − 12Dq.\n\n**Why ν₁ alone is not used.** Setting 10Dq = 4 330 gives Dq = 433 cm⁻¹. The ⁴T₁ matrix then gives B ≈ 878 cm⁻¹ from the eigenvalue sum. The eigenvalue product does not agree with that value, so the three bands are not consistent with Dq = 433.\n\n**Fit to ν₂ and ν₃.** The eigenvalue sum gives:\n- ν₂ + ν₃ = 26 160 = 30Dq + 15B, so B = 1 744 − 2Dq.\n\nThe eigenvalue product gives:\n- (7 520 − 12Dq)(18 640 − 12Dq) = 90Dq·B − 36B²\n\nSubstituting B and simplifying gives 117Dq² − 180 504Dq + 62 417 024 = 0. The root that applies is Dq ≈ 523 cm⁻¹, which gives B ≈ 697 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Check.** These values predict ν₁ = 10Dq ≈ 5 230 cm⁻¹, against 4 330 observed. The mismatch of about 900 cm⁻¹ is large. Likely causes are spin–orbit coupling, a distorted geometry, or ν₁ being measured imprecisely. The Dq and B above should therefore be treated as approximate.\n\n{\"Dq\": 523, \"B\": 697, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Fit of the two ⁴T₁ bands in the tetrahedral d7 model gives Dq≈523 and B≈697 cm⁻¹, but the predicted ν1 (≈5230) misses the observed 4330 cm⁻¹, so values are approximate.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens